      "writtenOn": "2026-05-12T12:43:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not with this change:\n\npolygerrit-ui/app/elements/change/gr-change-summary/gr-change-summary.ts\n```typescript\nprivate get canShowAiReview(): boolean {\n  return !!this.selfAccount \u0026\u0026 this.canAiReview;\n}\n```\n\nWith this condition, both AI related actions (\"Create AI Review Prompt\" and \"AI Chat\") are only shown to authenticated users and remain hidden for anonymous users.",
      "parentUuid": "67adc9dc_05f79b67",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 239,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 241,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "0611e357f4f2c5fffaaf8d545ee980b5d66a2e87",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4df1154c_d3dbca0c",
        "filename": "polygerrit-ui/app/elements/change/gr-change-summary/gr-change-summary.ts",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 123,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-13T10:09:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This isn\u0027t very readable to me. Why not check for `undefined`?\n\n\n\n```suggestion\n    return this.selfAccount !\u003d\u003d undefined \u0026\u0026 this.canAiReview;\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 123,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 123,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "0611e357f4f2c5fffaaf8d545ee980b5d66a2e87",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "65a66a8e_e251c4b5",
        "filename": "polygerrit-ui/app/elements/change/gr-change-summary/gr-change-summary.ts",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 123,
      "author": {
        "id": 1011323
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-13T11:43:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think `!!this.selfAccount` is intentional here: it checks whether `selfAccount` is truthy before showing the AI review option.\n\nReplacing it with `this.selfAccount !\u003d\u003d undefined` is not equivalent, because `null !\u003d\u003d undefined` is true while `!!null` is false. Unless the type guarantees that `selfAccount` can never be null, I’d prefer to keep the current boolean guard.\n\nI also checked usage in polygerrit-ui/app: explicit undefined checks appear 121 times, while !!... truthiness checks appear 379 times, so the current style does not seem unusual in the polygerrit codebase.",
      "parentUuid": "4df1154c_d3dbca0c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 123,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 123,
        "endChar": 29
      },
